    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n116013" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψωρ-ιάω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>to have the itch, scab,</i> or <i>mange,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Aph.</u>
				4.77
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.126b
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψ. τὴν κύστιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Dsc.
					3.151
				</span></i>
			, 
				v.l. for
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψωράω</span>
			 in <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Grg.</u>
				494c
			</span></i>; of dogs, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Gp.</u>
				19.3.2
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> of trees,
				<i>to be scabby, cankered,</i> esp. of the fig, <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>CP</u>
				5.9.10
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>HP</u>
				4.14.3
			</span></i>, etc.; of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κύμινον,</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				8.10.1
			</span></i>.</div>
